   <p style=3D'margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:5pt;font-family:"Comic Sans MS";
   font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-US>Great question, Dhrubo — and right up y=
our
   alley given your deep dive into processor architecture and networking. T=
he <span
   style=3D'font-weight:bold'>Data Path</span> and <span style=3D'font-weig=
ht:bold'>Control
   Path</span> are the two foundational subsystems inside a CPU or
   microcomputer. They work together to execute instructions, but each has a
   distinct role. Let’s break them down:</p>
   <p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:14.0pt' lang=3Den-U=
S>&nbsp;</p>
   <h2 style=3D'margin:0in;font-size:14.0pt;color:#2E75B5' lang=3Den-US><sp=
an
   style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji"'>&#129504;</span><span style=3D'fo=
nt-family:
